 If your child stands on the sidelines at the playground, they may not be unfriendly—they may just not know how to join in.

For many shy kids, walking up to a group feels overwhelming.

Instead of saying, **"Just go ask if you can play,"** help them practice simple conversation starters that make joining in feel more natural.

Try phrases like:

💬 "What are you guys playing?"

💬 "Need another player?"

💬 "Can I be on a team?"

💬 "That looks fun—how do you play?"

💬 "I like that game. Can I try?"

Practice these at home through role-play so they become familiar before your child needs them.

Your child may still feel nervous—and that's okay.

Confidence isn't about never feeling shy.

It's about having the tools to take the first small step.
